50ea47f50152c0162dbd21aeb84df8d40781fa816d711f9051","archived":false,"result":{"passes":{"finder":{}}}},{"cellId":"qodo-lockbox:074/r1/focal/w-musewonder-xhigh","status":"ok","source":"qodo-finder-1055/out-lockbox-w/25bd54588e11fdedb2cd4dc08c2669a7a21a60b166b20b518dd198bb813c5fe4/raw/105e843a3f37f51c949f35ffcc70a9ba3deb80173dbdde9debd26200cbb08efe.json","sourceSha256":"206352d301c7aa60eb5ead0207bbd7ddd5029b6841ba6806a7d69ec028f0e33f","archived":false,"result":{"bindings":{"commandBuffer":0,"commandDeadline":0,"finderDeadline":false,"grepClipped":0,"harnessProjection":0,"providerMax":0,"tokenProjection":0},"checkout":{"baseSha":"61b7f8fc29757e6d38f1949fbae90dfc2e90ccf3","headSha":"0bc01a435076c95c4c001445b9c179f3816470b2","wallMs":3757.772},"publication":{"cap":null,"open":10,"published":10,"severityFloor":null,"total":10},"review":{"confidence":0.82,"findings":[{"description":"The status field is hardcoded to trigger.expect, unlike FlowRunStateTriggerFields (lines 24-25) and the new DeploymentStatusTriggerFields (lines 30-31), which use trigger.after when posture is Proactive (\"Stays in\"). With after empty, the backend only creates a bucket when the expected status event itself arrives and increments it toward threshold, so at the default threshold of 1 a Proactive trigger can never fire for absence/staying in that status. Fix by selecting the field name from posture like the sibling components.","failureMode":"A Proactive work-pool status automation created in the wizard never fires at the default threshold.","file":"ui-v2/src/components/automations/automations-wizard/trigger-step/work-pool-status-trigger-fields.tsx","line":36,"severity":"high","side":"RIGHT","title":"Work-pool Proactive status writes to expect instead of after"},{"description":"The status field is hardcoded to trigger.expect, unlike FlowRunStateTriggerFields (lines 24-25) and the new DeploymentStatusTriggerFields (lines 30-31), which use trigger.after when posture is Proactive (\"Stays in\"). With after empty, the backend only creates a bucket when the expected status event itself arrives and increments it toward threshold, so at the default threshold of 1 a Proactive trigger can never fire for absence/staying in that status. Fix by selecting the field name from posture like the sibling components.","failureMode":"A Proactive work-queue status automation created in the wizard never fires at the default threshold.","file":"ui-v2/src/components/automations/automations-wizard/trigger-step/work-queue-status-trigger-fields.tsx","line":36,"severity":"high","side":"RIGHT","title":"Work-queue Proactive status writes to expect instead of after"},{"description":"The field name switches between trigger.after and trigger.expect, but nothing clears or migrates the previously selected value, and PostureSelect and the wizard onSubmit apply no cleanup. Selecting Ready while Reactive, switching to Proactive, and submitting (or selecting another status) submits both the stale expect=[prefect.deployment.ready] and the new after value even though the UI shows only one placeholder/status. Fix by clearing or moving the other field when posture changes.","endLine":31,"failureMode":"Switching posture after picking a status submits a trigger containing a status the UI no longer displays.","file":"ui-v2/src/components/automations/automations-wizard/trigger-step/deployment-status-trigger-fields.tsx","line":30,"severity":"medium","side":"RIGHT","title":"Deployment posture switch leaves stale expect/after values"},{"description":"String.split never returns an empty array: verified that ''.split('\\n') is [''] and 'a\\n'.split('\\n') is ['a',''], so the lines.length check is dead and clearing the textarea or ending with a newline stores an empty-string event in trigger.expect. That bogus entry passes the zod array-of-strings schema and is submitted as an expected event. Fix by filtering out empty/blank lines (and returning undefined when none remain).","endLine":39,"failureMode":"Clearing the custom events field or trailing a newline submits an empty-string expected event instead of no events.","file":"ui-v2/src/components/automations/automations-wizard/trigger-step/custom-trigger-fields.tsx","line":38,"severity":"medium","side":"RIGHT","title":"Custom events textarea stores empty-string events"},{"description":"This changes strict from true (base revision) to false, weakening the tsc -b --noEmit validate:types gate for the whole ui-v2 app and violating the repository mandate requiring strict type checking. Null/undefined and implicit-any errors that previously failed validation will now pass and can reach runtime. Fix by restoring strict: true and fixing any type errors it surfaces in the new code.","failureMode":"Type errors across ui-v2 that strict mode previously rejected now pass validation and can crash at runtime.","file":"ui-v2/tsconfig.app.json","line":19,"severity":"medium","side":"RIGHT","title":"TypeScript strict mode disabled"},{"description":"This threshold handler uses the global parseInt without a radix while every sibling uses Number(...) and the rest of ui-v2 uses Number.parseInt(value, 10); biome.json sets style/useNumberNamespace to error, so biome check fails on this line. It also differs behaviorally: verified parseInt('') is NaN while Number('') is 0, so clearing the field stores NaN instead of a validatable number. Fix by using Number(e.target.value) like the other trigger fields.","failureMode":"The lint gate fails on this line and clearing the work-pool threshold stores NaN in the form.","file":"ui-v2/src/components/automations/automations-wizard/trigger-step/work-pool-status-trigger-fields.tsx","line":78,"severity":"low","side":"RIGHT","title":"Global parseInt violates lint rule and yields NaN on clear"},{"description":"Repository mandate 10 requires a component.test.tsx beside each component file, as flow-run-state-trigger-fields.test.tsx does for the sibling component. Listing the trigger-step directory shows only flow-run-state-trigger-fields.test.tsx and trigger-step.test.tsx, with no custom-trigger-fields.test.tsx for this new component. Fix by adding the co-located test file covering its event-text conversion.","failureMode":"The new custom trigger component ships without its mandated co-located test, leaving its textarea conversion without dedicated regression coverage.","file":"ui-v2/src/components/automations/automations-wizard/trigger-step/custom-trigger-fields.tsx","line":14,"severity":"low","side":"RIGHT","title":"Missing co-located test for CustomTriggerFields"},{"description":"Repository mandate 10 requires a component.test.tsx beside each component file, as flow-run-state-trigger-fields.test.tsx does for the sibling component. Listing the trigger-step directory shows only flow-run-state-trigger-fields.test.tsx and trigger-step.test.tsx, with no deployment-status-trigger-fields.test.tsx for this new component. Fix by adding the co-located test file covering its posture-dependent status field.","failureMode":"The new deployment status component ships without its mandated co-located test, leaving its posture field switching without dedicated regression coverage.","file":"ui-v2/src/components/automations/automations-wizard/trigger-step/deployment-status-trigger-fields.tsx","line":25,"severity":"low","side":"RIGHT","title":"Missing co-located test for DeploymentStatusTriggerFields"},{"description":"Repository mandate 10 requires a component.test.tsx beside each component file, as flow-run-state-trigger-fields.test.tsx does for the sibling component. Listing the trigger-step directory shows only flow-run-state-trigger-fields.test.tsx and trigger-step.test.tsx, with no work-pool-status-trigger-fields.test.tsx for this new component. Fix by adding the co-located test file covering its status and threshold fields.","failureMode":"The new work-pool status component ships without its mandated co-located test, leaving its status and threshold behavior without dedicated regressi